.SS "Minor Changes"
.IP "\(bu" 2
Add a new \fRfuture\&.v7_fetcherPersist\fP flag to the \fR@remix-run/router\fP to change the persistence behavior of fetchers when \fRrouter\&.deleteFetcher\fP is called\&. Instead of being immediately cleaned up, fetchers will persist until they return to an \fRidle\fP state (\fRRFC\fP) (\fR#10962\fP)
.IP "  \(bu" 4
This is sort of a long-standing bug fix as the \fRuseFetchers()\fP API was always supposed to only reflect \fBin-flight\fP fetcher information for pending/optimistic UI -- it was not intended to reflect fetcher data or hang onto fetchers after they returned to an \fRidle\fP state
.IP "  \(bu" 4
Keep an eye out for the following specific behavioral changes when opting into this flag and check your app for compatibility:
.IP "    \(bu" 6
Fetchers that complete \fIwhile still mounted\fP will no longer appear in \fRuseFetchers()\fP\&. They served effectively no purpose in there since you can access the data via \fRuseFetcher()\&.data\fP)\&.
.IP "    \(bu" 6
Fetchers that previously unmounted \fIwhile in-flight\fP will not be immediately aborted and will instead be cleaned up once they return to an \fRidle\fP state\&. They will remain exposed via \fRuseFetchers\fP while in-flight so you can still access pending/optimistic data after unmount\&.
.PP

.PP

.IP "\(bu" 2
When \fRv7_fetcherPersist\fP is enabled, the router now performs ref-counting on fetcher keys via \fRgetFetcher\fP/\fRdeleteFetcher\fP so it knows when a given fetcher is totally unmounted from the UI (\fR#10977\fP)
.IP "  \(bu" 4
Once a fetcher has been totally unmounted, we can ignore post-processing of a persisted fetcher result such as a redirect or an error
.IP "  \(bu" 4
The router will also pass a new \fRdeletedFetchers\fP array to the subscriber callbacks so that the UI layer can remove associated fetcher data
.PP

